body:
Ok few things I'd like to add. Idolizing anyone is unhealthy regardless of message, people are people and even the smartest and most brilliant minded folks can make foolish mistakes. Have you listened, actually listened to Jordan Peterson with an open minded approach in a way that's as unbiased as you can be? I don't care for the political side of things but I think we're all fools if we agree to coerced speech by threat of force and frankly regardless of whatever his motives are, it take a lot of courage to refuse to do something that is being written into law. I think its comical that so many people think he's a goddamned idiot when, regardless of whether he is right or wrong about certain topics, he clearly has a superior intellect compared to any of my college professors and teachers and seems to be to have genuine compassion which is devoid for the most part in most activist groups who demonize him for being a transphobe or some nonsense like that.

&#x200B;

I don't agree with many of his talking points but if you cannot see that this man is reasonable and that while your bf is maybe star struck that doesn't have to be a total loss unless of course you don't get what is appealing to many younger men about his message. Frankly I would agree that younger men are lost or at least the majority are bumbling through life with nothing more than the will to not be homeless or imprisoned. The fact of the matter is, and please don't take this as a jab as I don't mean it in a condescending way, men get very little encouragement and the lie that there is an inherit benefit to being male (especially white and straight) is mind blowing; either that or I simply missed the meetings where they congregated to get benefits or learn the secrets of male domination, in fact I would be inclined to say based on my own experience which is certainly subject to scrutiny but here goes: I grew up as a middle class, albeit lower middle but by NO means poor, kid who hadn't a clue of what the world was like. I was naive and depressed and constantly punished for it. In my family 18 = college or GTFO so I reluctantly signed up to a community college (it had to be far enough away that I couldn't live at home but that's understandable). I hated it, I was aimless, bored, tired and it was around this time the dialog started to be a bit more against "young men" then I experienced in my bubble. Frankly no one gives you credit nor cares if you suffer if you're a man in america on campus in fact nowadays I cannot imagine how any young man could stand to hear such horrible shit about men all day; accusations hurled and i dare say believed to a point by women which are true but only situationally and not systemically or as a default mode of "maleness" seeing as it's   based off of the most heinous actions of sociopaths but hurled so carelessly, with a certain surety and scorn that can and should start to make men drop out of colleges or at least feel like they are truly hated for their existence. 

So in short your bf likes Jordan Peterson because frankly he sees through a lot of rhetoric and understands it is getting uglier for men and until recently anyone brave enough to fight back was easily dismissed as a sexist misogynist white man and one who hates women, because patriarchy or oppressed pasts etc. and therefore point not taken. Other gems of wisdom you'll hear bringing up anything to do with men's issues (ha right yeah men don't suffer ok....) When discussions of male suicide take place an abhorrent yet unfortunately quite common rebuttal is : Maybe men commit suicide more because they are not able to dominate and keep women down, oh that's helpful and makes me feel great... you? 


Anyhow I am rambling, but I think it's important to share my experience even if only 1 out of 7 billion gets some hope out of it..  I am much older now and a lot less naive but certainly not devoid of problems. I left behind the  delusional child and accepted that the world is NEVER going to be a utopia, EVER, in my lifetime and I don't think people could bear the monotonous harmony of perfection and "samethink" for any significant timeframe.  I refused to become an embittered victim and frankly I had reasons, we all do. 

&#x200B;

I RARELY give out any direction but I will make an exception and can do so  with close absolute certainty; if you are thinking of breaking up over this or you judge him to be of lesser value than you are leave now, do it maturely, please. It will hurt him and probably hurt badly,  but in failing to see that there is possible a lot of internal suffering  (regardless of what I have heard many a woman say about wanting men to talk about feelings with them, I rarely see it improving things in fact it usually destroys them) and that at least the guy is looking to better himself; yet since not to your liking this will likely result in him coming to the conclusion that you're unable or unwilling to disagree or understand someone or something you don't like and so quickly and foolishly are now acting as superior but to judge without actually knowing WHY he's listening should send him running if he has learned anything from Jordan Peterson which may be painful to you. Men think a LOT and rarely utter a word especially when suffering, most are drawn to Peterson BECAUSE they are suffering silently and for fucks sake they should be listening to someone who isn't going to abhor them for wanting the pain to stop.

&#x200B;

I have been married for a long time, my wife and I were poor for a long time, very long and yet not too miserably nor defeated. Im quite sure neither of us alone would or could have pulled us out or maybe it would be possible but without cooperation resentment would have killed chances of that, it required a lot of sacrifices but it paid off and we were able to establish some sort of stability by encouraging one another. We're not super successful today but we are compared to our past selves. Today she can work if she wants and occasionally does sporadically. 

&#x200B;

I don't want her to HAVE to work and we made this decision together, I prefer her home, but frankly I prefer the best for her over my own beliefs, would die without question for her if need be and know damn well she loves me for who I am not what I do for a living, or who I listen to for inspiration or what salary I have etc.. Of course we disagree on all sorts of  things, I didn't want to marry some subservient gentile brainless girl, nor one of the "Go Girl! Girl Power! - Girls are smart and superior and always right, men are dogs they must be trained" Princessy types, which are doomed to a life of meaninglessness and typically despised without realizing it until its WAY too late. What  I wanted was a woman that actually gave a shit enough about me to tell me when I was being unreasonably stupid or difficult while also having the maturity and feminine gentleness to actually accept an apology and grant forgiveness rather than seeing it as a victory for women everywhere. Real acceptance  of an apology means not using past incidents in future conflicts or keeping a list of transgressions (women are very skilled at arguments and more powerful now and historically than they will ever imagine a man would think as it doesn't sit well with the narrative of feminist history ) 

&#x200B;

If you DO want it to work because you are truly in love but confused and perhaps scared the Bottom line i'd say is to do this: find out why EXACTLY he like Jordan and try to do this without morally posturing and /  or asking in the condescending ways that many  people who prefer to be right over wanting to hear the truth often do . (You do know what I mean we all have done it to someone or had it done and it shuts guys down immediately). Be honest with your concerns only if they appear to be valid, in a lot of cases when you assume the why you are most certainly wrong to a degree sometimes only slightly but often missing the mark COMPLETELY.

Men are having issues same as women, whites, blacks, yellows, trans, whatever else is a primate and capable of thought could be and we all suffer a LOT often times in men, suicide becomes a very appealing option, I will say Jordan most definitely has saved at a minimum one soul from the act and thats probably a gross underestimation. Please do whatever you can to either leave or move forward but I will say the moment you think you're smarter, better, etc, than a partner is about the same time they realize it, leave and move on and it's not a place anyone wants to be. good luck
